add(dict(id=pid,title='Discriminate thermal and instantaneous nonlinear optical response',objective='Test instantaneous electronic, thermal-memory and mixed models against the same time/power observations for the INP solutions under the reported experimental conditions, and determine whether their contributions are identifiable.',objects={'INP_solution_data':obj('INP_solution',0,(1,),identity_file='inp_molecule.json',note='Physical response dataset, not an electronic spin calculation; charge/multiplicity are reporting placeholders for this dataset object.')},keep_files=['inp_molecule.json'],status='blocked',blockers=['A traceable table of independent N(t), power/intensity and Z-scan measured points with digitization errors has not been prepared from main Figures 6, 9–10 and SI S8. Smooth fitted curves and the reported fitted time constants are not independent observations.','The available source text does not establish a complete calibrated SSPM beam-waist, instrument-response and thermal-parameter dataset. Obtain measurement/plot digitization with bounded parameter provenance before completing model discrimination.'],boundary='Use the source INP solution concentrations 0.25, 0.50 and 1.0 mM, CW 532 nm, 1 mm cell, with 50 mW temporal SSPM and power scans up to 150 mW. These are solution conditions; do not pool the separate 0.4 mm PMMA film. Source experimental solvent and beam/thermal quantities must be carried from a verified data table; no aqueous solvent is inferred from the dye name. The old isolated-molecule frontier gap is optional background only.',reference_definition='All three physical models share the same measured observation rows, concentration/path-length/absorption/beam definitions and measurement uncertainty. Fit data and held-out conditions are disjoint; no synthetic or interpolated points count as measurements.',conditions={'Z_scan_beam_waist_um':16,'Z_scan_Rayleigh_length_mm':1.51,'wavelength_nm':532,'solution_thickness_mm':1,'concentrations_mM':[0.25,0.5,1.0],'linear_absorption_cm_inverse':[3.22,6.9,7.36],'temporal_input_power_mW':50,'power_scan_max_mW':150,'thermal_parameters':'Missing calibrated source/prior ranges; not invented','source':'Main PDF p3, p9, Figures6/9/10; SI p7 S8'},controls={'instantaneous':'Memoryless phase proportional to intensity with the measured beam/instrument-response convolution.','thermal':'Heat equation or explicitly justified reduced diffusion response driven by absorbed power alpha, path length and beam radius. Share material parameters across conditions.','mixed':'Sum of electronic and thermal contributions under the same calibration. Parameter profiles may establish a non-identifiable range.','validation':'Hold out one measured power/concentration/time condition before fitting; never use author fitted tau as held-out raw data.'},panels={'observations':panel(O(measured_points=A(O(dataset_id=S(),time_s=N(),power_mW=N(minimum=0),concentration_mM=E([0.25,0.5,1.0]),observable=E(['ring_count','normalized_transmittance','ring_radius_mm']),value=N(),uncertainty=N(minimum=0),source_page_figure=S(),digitization_file=PATH),6),beam_waist_m=N(minimum=0),thickness_m=N(minimum=0),instrument_response_file=PATH,thermal_parameter_bounds_file=PATH),'Verified observation and physical-parameter table','Verify points against source plot pixels/raw measurements and uncertainty. Do not count resampling or fitted curves as additional observations. Check intensity I0=2P/(pi w0^2) only when that beam-waist convention is appropriate and traceable.'),'model_comparison':panel(K(['instantaneous','thermal','mixed'],fit),'Same-data constrained comparison of three physical models','Inspect executable equations and fitted outputs; check consistent shared parameters, residual weighting, data splits and degrees of freedom. Per-curve unconstrained constants cannot establish a thermal/electronic decomposition.'),'identifiability':panel(O(parameter_profile_file=PATH,correlation_matrix=A(A(N())),electronic_fraction_interval=A(N(),2),held_out_predictions_file=PATH,held_out_residuals_file=PATH,memory_test=PAIR,identified=E(['unique_within_bounds','bounded_equivalence','models_rejected']),evidence_files=EV),'Identifiability, history dependence and held-out prediction','Read parameter profile and held-out residuals. A finite accepted interval must derive from real noisy data and constraints, not a point fit. Allow evidence-backed non-identifiability, but missing measurements are incomplete.')},investigations={'observations':'Assemble and validate a measurement table with provenance and digitization/beam/thermal bounds. Resolve the current input gate before scientific fitting.','model_comparison':'Fit all three physically defined responses jointly under one calibration; preserve residuals and code, including any model rejection.','identifiability':'Profile the mixed fraction and key correlated parameters, test rise-time/history dependence, and predict held-out conditions. Report bounded equivalence if justified.'},author='The authors discuss strong CW nonlinear response primarily as thermal lensing. Main p3 defines Z-scan/SSPM phase and absorption quantities; main pp9–10 describes time-dependent rings and compares the two optical techniques. The isolated INP B3LYP/6-311G(d,p) frontier-orbital argument in the source does not resolve thermal/electronic contributions. The benchmark joint model comparison, shared-parameter constraints and withheld-condition test are new and must use measured points, not the authors fitted constants.',pitfalls='Reject synthetic measurement tables, arbitrary three-curve fitting, inference of bulk n2 from a HOMO-LUMO gap, pooling film and solution, or declaring unique electronic fractions without parameter identifiability.',optional='Molecular DFT, PMMA-film modeling and optical limiter performance are optional.',source_note='Read main pp3 and 9–11, Figures6/9/10 and SI pp6–7 S7/S8. Main p11 states data available on request; this audit has not contacted authors. The plotted time/power curves are present but an uncertainty-bearing measurement dataset and full beam/thermal calibration are not yet prepared. Status is explicitly blocked.',software='Existing Python/SciPy environment; no quantum-chemical engine is necessary for the minimum task.',pilot='First audit measured rows, units and time resolution; fit a shared thermal response and compute a parameter-profile rank/identifiability check before requiring a contribution fraction.',reference_gaps=['Digitized real measurement table and traceable beam/thermal bounds are needed.','No fitted expanded reference, residual distribution or noise-based tolerance has been computed.']))

