add(dict(id=a,title='Resolve donor position, torsion and excited-state character in three TADF candidates',objective='Test whether donor type and placement alter singlet–triplet proximity through charge-transfer localization, geometric relaxation or both, while retaining optically active states.',objects={k:obj(f,identity_file=k+'_identity.json') for k,f in [('TD_2T','C72H49N7'),('CD_2T','C72H47N7'),('TD_2C','C72H45N7')]},boundary='Use the supplied complete mapped graphs. The common dibenzo[f,h]pyrazino[2,3-b]quinoxaline core has donor sites 3,6,11: TD_2T has triphenylamine at all three; CD_2T has phenylcarbazole at 11; TD_2C has phenylcarbazole at 3 and 6. All are neutral. Use a consistent gas-phase baseline, singlet ground states and singlet/triplet excited states. No author optimized geometries, CT assignments or predicted gaps are supplied.',reference_definition='Vertical gap=E(S1;R_S0)-E(T1;R_S0); adiabatic gap=E(S1;R_S1)-E(T1;R_T1). Do not mix these or use Kohn–Sham gaps as excitation gaps. SOC is the norm of three spin components in cm^-1 with operator and state basis stated.',controls={'conformers':'At least two independently initialized donor torsion patterns per molecule; document retention or convergence to the same minimum.','fixed_torsion':'For all three molecules freeze the three core–linker torsions at 45 degrees and relax other S0 coordinates. Define each four-atom torsion using the common core numbering and mapped linker ortho carbon; carry a signed orientation convention. This is a benchmark intervention, not a claimed minimum.','state_tracking':'Compute at least S1,S2,T1,T2 and enlarge the root window to demonstrate state matching. Compare NTO/density overlap and identical core/three-donor partitions.','relaxation':'Obtain state-followed S1 and T1 relaxed energies for each molecule; avoid root-switching into another excited state.'},panels={'vertical_matrix':panel(K(['TD_2T','CD_2T','TD_2C'],K(['relaxed_S0','fixed_torsion'],exc)),'Six matched vertical-state and SOC panels','Check graph and donor position rather than inconsistent SI product prose. Recompute gaps, fragment weights and SOC norms. State roots must be tracked by densities. A small gap alone is not mechanistic proof.'),'relaxation_matrix':panel(K(['TD_2T','CD_2T','TD_2C'],O(conformer_attempts=REF,selected_record=S(),S0_energy_Eh=N(),S1_record=S(),T1_record=S(),S1_energy_Eh=N(),T1_energy_Eh=N(),adiabatic_gap_eV=N(),state_matching_file=PATH,evidence_files=EV)),'Conformer and excited-geometry discrimination','Verify S1/T1 energies and geometries on consistent surfaces; inspect conformer outcomes. A collapsed state must be evidenced and alternative starts examined; no invented state minimum.'),'causal_comparison':panel(K(['donor_change_at_11','donor_change_at_3_6','torsion_relaxation_effect'],PAIR),'Position versus geometry and method robustness','Use like-defined transition observables at common conditions. Report what fixed torsion does and does not isolate; multiple donor replacements are not equivalent to a single-site substitution. Require a CT-sensitive method or solvent sensitivity with actual calculations.')},investigations={'vertical_matrix':'Generate independently initialized conformers, build the common torsion intervention, and calculate energies, oscillator strengths, fragment-resolved transition densities and SOC for matched low states in all six cells.','relaxation_matrix':'Follow S1 and T1 relaxation for each member and explicitly separate vertical and adiabatic gaps. Preserve conformer and root-switch diagnostics.','causal_comparison':'Compare changes at site 11 and sites 3/6, then quantify the shift from fixed to relaxed torsions and a decisive method sensitivity. Evaluate both CT-based and geometry-based explanations.'},author='The authors use B3LYP/6-31G(d,p) in Gaussian09 and NTO analysis in Multiwfn3.8, and attribute TADF differences to donor substitution and excited-state character. Main Figure1 and SI synthesis headings/HRMS define the structures. SI theoretical methods prints 6-31(d), and some synthesis reagent/product labels conflict with the correctly named headings and formulas; do not silently interpret these as new molecules. The common torsion, independent conformer and direct SOC comparisons are new benchmark tests. Device EQE is outside this molecular calculation.',pitfalls='Reject swapped CD/TD donor layouts, unequal state/solvent definitions, root-index-only matches, missing SOC or oscillator evidence, or an OLED efficiency claim based solely on a molecular gap.',optional='OLED host/device modeling, absolute RISC rates and additional donor series are optional.',source_note='Read main pp2–5, Figure1 molecular layouts and excited-state analysis; official publisher SI sections I/II, S3–S6 and TableS1. Verified three systematic names with OPSIN and RDKit formulas C72H49N7/C72H47N7/C72H45N7. SI has mislabeled intermediates, a copied TD-2C product name and ambiguous basis shorthand; heading structures and HRMS resolve connectivity, not calculated state assignments.',software='Gaussian or ORCA for DFT/TDDFT and supported SOC; Multiwfn or documented equivalent for transition densities.',pilot='Check each graph/formula and one two-conformer TD_2T calculation, SOC interface and root matching before the six-cell comparison.',reference_gaps=['No new fixed-torsion, conformer, SOC or adiabatic reference matrix has been calculated.','Resolve basis shorthand explicitly and calibrate CT-state/method uncertainty.']))

