add(dict(id=pid,title='Distinguish spin–phonon tensor coupling from mode occupation in Y2 cages',objective='Determine whether lateral Y–Y motion has distinctive spin–phonon coupling relative to longitudinal and cage motion, and separate tensor derivatives from thermal mode weighting in the two cage isomers.',objects={k:obj('C87H7Y2',0,(2,),identity_file=f) for k,f in [('Ih','y2_ih.xyz'),('D5h','y2_d5h.xyz')]},keep_files=['y2_ih.xyz','y2_d5h.xyz'],boundary='Retain the complete 96-atom molecules, including the C87H7 adduct and two Y atoms (source XYZ rows 81 and 82, one-based). Both neutral molecules have a doublet electronic state. This is a molecular EPR-tensor task; a Gd substitution is not an equivalent electronic model.',reference_definition='In a common molecule-fixed Cartesian frame, dT/dQ=[T(+h)-T(-h)]/(2h) for T=g or hyperfine A, with mass-weighted normal coordinate Q and units declared. Compare h/2. Report n=1/(exp(hc nu/kT)-1) and n(n+1) separately from the derivative-based coupling; use positive vibrational frequencies.',controls={'modes':'Normalize Y relative displacements with the equilibrium Y–Y axis. Report the four largest lateral-projection modes per cage and select one representative lateral, longitudinal and cage-dominated mode for tensor derivatives. Projection selection precedes looking at derivatives.','finite_difference':'For each selected mode compute +/-h and +/-h/2 at the same electronic method; hold geometry otherwise fixed.','orientation':'Rigidly rotate one displaced/undisplaced set, rotate the tensor back with R^T T R and verify invariance. Do not finite-difference independently sorted principal values near degeneracy.','thermal':'Use 20 K and 100 K as common comparison temperatures, with occupation and derivative contributions reported separately.'},panels={'mode_assignment':panel(K(['Ih','D5h'],O(reference_record=S(),hessian_file=PATH,lateral_candidates=A(O(mode_index=I(1),frequency_cm1=N(),projection=N(minimum=0)),4),projection_table_file=PATH,axis=VEC,evidence_files=EV)),'Mode eigenvectors and reproducible displacement classification','Inspect mass normalization, removed rigid modes, Y–Y axis and projection table. Frequency agreement without eigenvectors is insufficient.'),'tensor_derivatives':panel(K(['Ih','D5h'],K(['lateral','longitudinal','cage'],deriv)),'Six central tensor derivatives with step control','Recalculate finite differences from raw tensors and mode normalization. Keep frames and spin states consistent. Require real smaller-step outputs; check electronic noise relative to derivative signal.'),'thermal_and_frame_controls':panel(O(temperature_rows=A(O(cage=E(['Ih','D5h']),mode_index=I(1),temperature_K=E([20,100]),bose_n=N(minimum=0),raman_weight=N(minimum=0),derivative_norm=N(minimum=0),weighted_proxy=N(minimum=0)),12),rotation_matrix=TENSOR,back_rotated_tensor=TENSOR,original_tensor=TENSOR,rotation_error=N(minimum=0),rotation_records=REF,lateral_vs_longitudinal=PAIR,lateral_vs_cage=PAIR,evidence_files=EV),'Occupation versus coupling and rotational covariance','Check n(n+1), same temperature and frequency units. Weighted derivative norm is a stated proxy, not a computed relaxation rate. A larger Bose factor alone does not identify a stronger spin–phonon interaction.')},investigations={'mode_assignment':'Optimize and validate both doublets, calculate modes and document projection-based assignment, including the four leading lateral candidates. Select three mode classes per cage by the declared rule.','tensor_derivatives':'Calculate a consistent g or A tensor for each central and four displaced geometries, retaining full components, normal coordinate units and spin-density validation.','thermal_and_frame_controls':'Perform the rigid-rotation check; compare bare derivative norms and thermal weights at both temperatures, and determine which mechanism explains differences between mode classes and cages.'},author='The source associates low-energy Y–Y motion with spin relaxation. Main pp8–10/Figure7 separates normal-mode character and thermal weighting. SI p2 uses PBE/def2-TZVP with a Dolg ECP for geometry and Hessian, but PBE-ZORA with ZORA-adjusted def2-TZVP for EPR properties; these are not identical calculations. SI pp20–26 reports spin–phonon and tensor evidence. The explicit mode-class negative controls, half-step and rigid-frame checks are benchmark extensions.',pitfalls='Reject singlet Y2 models, Gd substitution, wrong atom indices, occupation-only claims of coupling, inconsistent tensor frames/units, or interpreting these derivatives as measured T1/T2.',optional='Full relaxation-rate integration, all modes and Gd analogues are optional.',source_note='Read main pp3 and 8–10/Figure7, SI p2 computational methods and pp20–26 including TableS3 and S16/S17 figures. Checked final public coordinates: 96 atoms, C87H7Y2, Y rows81/82, neutral odd-electron state.',software='ORCA for open-shell DFT/Hessian and ZORA EPR tensors, Python/NumPy for mapped displacements and covariance.',pilot='Validate one cage doublet, one lateral eigenvector, a stable g/A tensor and h versus h/2 before extending mode classes.',reference_gaps=['No new mode projection matrix, negative-control derivatives or frame/step uncertainty reference has been run.']))

