add(dict(id=pid,title='Test competing electronic-state explanations for the full Ni complex',objective='Determine whether the full Ni complex supports a closed-shell description, a triplet or a distinct broken-symmetry state, and whether the conclusion survives geometry and electronic-method controls.',objects={'complex_4':obj('C87H72Cl2N2NiO',0,(1,3),identity_file='complex_4.xyz')},keep_files=['complex_4.xyz'],boundary='Use all 165 atoms in complex_4.xyz without ligand truncation. Retain neutral charge and the original connectivity; singlet, unrestricted broken-symmetry Ms=0 and triplet alternatives must be distinguished. A BS input multiplicity of 1 is not proof of a pure singlet.',reference_definition='Adiabatic electronic spin gap E(T;R_T)-E(CS;R_CS), separately from vertical E(T;R_CS)-E(CS;R_CS), in kcal/mol (1 hartree=627.509474 kcal/mol). No ZPE or G is folded into these E gaps. A collapsed BS attempt has no independent minimum energy.',controls={'spin_starts':'Initialize a closed-shell singlet, triplet and at least two distinct BS guesses (metal/ligand or opposite localized spin patterns); document densities, stability and collapse.','methods':'Repeat the decisive states with B3LYP and BP86 (or an explicitly equivalent calibrated two-method contrast) using the same basis partition and gas-phase condition.','geometry':'Compute vertical and relaxed differences, validate every claimed retained minimum and distinguish an SCF-stable wavefunction from a vibrational minimum.'},panels={'state_matrix':panel(K(['B3LYP','BP86'],O(closed_shell=spin,triplet=spin,broken_symmetry=spin_alt)),'Two-method electronic-state and stability matrix','Check independent BS initial densities and final density overlap/collapse. Spin occupations and populations must corroborate energy assignments. Failed convergence cannot be substituted for demonstrated collapse.'),'geometry_control':panel(K(['B3LYP','BP86'],O(CS_record=S(),triplet_vertical_record=S(),triplet_relaxed_record=S(),vertical_gap_kcal_mol=N(),adiabatic_gap_kcal_mol=N(),triplet_relaxation_kcal_mol=N(),bond_metrics_file=PATH,evidence_files=EV)),'Vertical versus relaxed spin energetics','Recompute matched electronic energy differences and relaxation term. Verify full structure, basis partition and stationarity; for 165 nonlinear atoms use 489 internal modes, not 495.'),'interpretation':panel(O(method_gap_contrast=PAIR,metal_spin_comparison_file=PATH,ligand_spin_comparison_file=PATH,occupation_comparison_file=PATH,electronic_description=E(['closed_shell_favored','triplet_favored','broken_symmetry_competitive','not_resolved']),evidence_files=EV),'Method robustness and metal–ligand electronic assignment','Use signed energy, stable wavefunctions, occupations and spin location together. Accept supported BS collapse and unresolved ordering, but reject an unattempted alternative or whole catalytic-cycle claims.')},investigations={'state_matrix':'Optimize/test CS, triplet and distinct BS starts at each method; retain stability, natural-orbital and spin-population outputs. Document any repeated convergence to the same state.','geometry_control':'Evaluate the triplet on the CS geometry and independently relax the triplet, validating geometries and comparing their electronic gaps.','interpretation':'Compare method-dependent gaps and occupations; test localized-metal versus ligand-radical descriptions against the actual spin densities.'},author='Main p4 and SI pp10–11 use B3LYP and BP86 with def2-TZVP on Ni and first-coordination-sphere atoms Cl1/Cl2/N1/N2/C1/C2 and def2-SVP elsewhere. The authors favor a closed-shell solution and report open-shell starts collapsing to it; their triplet comparison is an electronic-energy comparison. Toluene SMD used for optical calculations is a separate condition. The benchmark requires explicit independent BS, wavefunction stability and vertical/relaxed controls.',pitfalls='Reject truncated ligand/incorrect charge, a BS determinant identified as a spin-pure singlet, failed SCF called collapse, mixing electronic and thermal energies or different basis partitions, or claims about water-oxidation performance.',optional='Full water oxidation, additional catalyst substitutions and excited-state spectra are optional.',source_note='Read main p4 and SI pp10–11 computational/electronic-state discussion. Verified 165-atom full neutral complex formula and source method partition. Old isolated adiabatic scalar is only a baseline audit, not the new electronic-state matrix.',software='ORCA or Gaussian with unrestricted guesses, stability and population/natural-orbital output.',pilot='Map the source first coordination sphere, converge CS/triplet plus two BS starts with full model, then inspect wavefunction and vibrational stability.',reference_gaps=['New BS starts, stability/occupation evidence, BP86/B3LYP matched controls and their uncertainty remain uncomputed.']))

