add(dict(id=pid,title='Discriminate protonation and tautomer candidates with joint NMR and optical evidence',objective='Discover which bounded protonation/tautomer candidates, or mixtures, can jointly explain the measured acid/base optical and NMR response of 2a, while testing solvent and proton-reference sensitivity.',objects={'parent_2a':obj('C30H20N6O4',0,(1,),identity_file='parent_identity.json'),'candidate_2a':obj('',0,(1,),charges=[-2,-1,0,1,2],identity_file='candidate_seeds.json',formula_rule='C30H(20+proton_change)N6O4; charge=proton_change; heavy atoms fixed')},boundary='Use the neutral mapped C30H20N6O4 parent and explicit candidate seed edits. Do not use former acidic/basic optimized coordinates, which are private. Preserve heavy-atom connectivity, allowing stated proton/bond tautomer rearrangements; charge must equal added proton count for this H+ exchange space. NMR is in DMSO-d6 and optical observations are in the separately reported aqueous pH conditions; compute each in its matching medium rather than treating them as the same solvent.',reference_definition='Within a fixed proton count compare like-solvated relative G. Across proton counts use a balanced proton-exchange cycle with a declared common acid/base reference and pH chemical-potential convention; raw different-charge total energies are not population rankings. Joint NMR/UV residuals use one predeclared error model per observable across all candidates.',observations={'source':'Main Table1/Figure3 and NMR discussion pp5–6; experimental observations, not calculated answers','optical':[{'condition':'acid','lambda_max_nm':350},{'condition':'base','lambda_max_nm':440}],'NMR_aromatic_site_ortho_to_terminal_OH':[{'condition':'acid','delta_ppm':6.80},{'condition':'neutral','delta_ppm':6.95},{'condition':'base','delta_ppm':6.10}],'conditions':{'optical_solvent':'water','NMR_solvent':'DMSO-d6','reported_condition_labels':['pH2','pH7','pH14'],'reported_pKa':9.89},'uncertainty':'Source does not provide per-point measurement errors; do not invent precision-based acceptance windows. Calibrate prediction uncertainty and disclose rounding/digitization.'},controls={'candidates':'Evaluate at least two distinct heteroatom protonation/bond-order classes under each acid/basic condition plus neutral parent, using candidate_seeds.json as minimum attempts. Include independent conformer starts and documented collapse.','spectra':'Predict both aromatic 1H shifts with an explicit shielding reference and allowed TD transitions in the corresponding solvents; select absorption features using oscillator strengths, not closest-energy matching.','protons':'Supply a balanced proton-exchange cycle for every cross-charge comparison. State acid/base reference species and solvation convention; test the decisive reference/solvent sensitivity.','mixtures':'A mixture is allowed only with normalized nonnegative populations and simultaneous fit of both observation types; extra free parameters need identifiability checks.'},panels={'candidate_registry':panel(O(candidates=A(candidate,5),parent_record=S(),atom_conservation_table_file=PATH),'Explicit proton/tautomer candidates and conformer evidence','Check charges, H counts, mapping, candidate classes and actual attempted geometries. Both acid and base must contain distinct site/bond alternatives; source endpoint relabeling is insufficient. Evidenced collapse may close a candidate, but missing convergence cannot.'),'joint_evidence':panel(O(comparisons=A(fitrow,4),uncertainty_model_file=PATH,shielding_calibration_file=PATH,spectral_assignment_file=PATH,populations=A(O(condition=E(['acid','neutral','base']),candidate_id=S(),weight=N(minimum=0)),3),joint_residual_analysis_file=PATH),'Joint NMR/UV discrimination','Check source observations and solvent mismatch carefully. Source NMR acidic assignment must be verified from the actual pH-labeled spectrum; author calculated acidic 7.98 ppm is not an experimental datum. All retained competing acid/base candidates require both predictions under identical calibration.'),'thermodynamic_and_robustness':panel(O(proton_cycles=A(O(candidate_id=S(),reaction=S(),species_charge_balance=C(0),delta_G_kcal_mol=N(),reference_species_records=REF,evidence_files=EV)),solvent_or_reference_contrast=PAIR,candidate_ordering_file=PATH,mixture_identifiability_file=PATH,evidence_files=EV),'Balanced speciation and robustness','Recompute cycle energies, charge/proton balances and populations. Gas-phase dianion artifacts do not invalidate a solvated state or prove it stable; distinguish electron binding, solvation and proton equilibria. Accept supported ambiguity after the complete candidate/spectral comparison.')},investigations={'candidate_registry':'Construct the supplied site and tautomer alternatives, add further symmetry-distinct candidates only when motivated, and document conformers, charges and bond/proton maps without presupposing the acid/base assignment.','joint_evidence':'Calculate matched-solvent NMR and UV predictions for all retained competitors; test individual and bounded-mixture interpretations with one uncertainty policy.','thermodynamic_and_robustness':'Close proton-reference cycles, compare populations consistently and repeat the decisive solvent/reference/model choice. Report only assignments supported jointly by both observations.'},author='Main computational methods uses CAM-B3LYP/6-31+G(d) in Gaussian16 with aqueous cLR-PCM for vertical excitations; formal SI includes DMSO NMR and acid/base structures. The authors interpret halochromism through protonation/deprotonation and show computed species and shifts. Those optimized structures/assignments are withheld from public data. The benchmark adds explicit alternative protonation/tautomer candidates and joint discrimination instead of accepting the two named source endpoints.',pitfalls='Reject answer geometries as discovered candidates, unequal atom counts without balanced cycles, source calculated shifts passed off as measurements, fitting each observable to unrelated species without a population model, or gas dianion failure called proof of solution instability.',optional='Cellulose sensor morphology, full pH dynamics, all substituted dyes and gas-phase dianion calculations are optional.',source_note='Read main computational methods p3, Table1, halochromic/NMR discussion pp4–6 and official SI acid/neutral/base NMR and coordinate blocks. Extracted only the neutral C30H20N6O4 graph. Source aqueous absorption and DMSO NMR require distinct solution models. Recheck exact acidic experimental NMR peak from Figure3 before freezing calibration; no expanded spectral/cycle reference exists.',software='Gaussian or ORCA DFT/TDDFT/NMR with diffuse functions and explicit solvent conventions; Python/RDKit for graph and mixture audits.',pilot='Check parent graph, two distinct acid/base seed valences and paired solvent calculations; validate NMR reference and proton-exchange convention before expanding.',reference_gaps=['New candidate energies, collapse checks, joint spectral residuals and balanced proton reference are uncomputed.','Experimental NMR assignment/rounding and observable uncertainty require final source-figure audit before reference freeze.']))

