high=O(geometry_record=S(),singlet_root_count=I(5),triplet_root_count=I(5),energy_window_eV=N(minimum=0),states=A(STATE,10),soc_pairs=A(SOC,3),state_map_file=PATH,fragment_map_file=PATH,evidence_files=EV)
add(dict(id=pid,title='Test high-triplet channel prerequisites with SOC, state tracking and competing states',objective='Determine whether proposed high-triplet singlet-transfer channels remain plausible after direct SOC, neighboring-state competition and geometric/method controls across the source emitter series.',objects={k:obj(f,0,(1,3),identity_file='molecular_identities.json') for k,f in [('Ph-mP','C34H24N2'),('Na-mP','C38H26N2'),('An-mP','C42H28N2'),('Py-mP','C44H28N2')]},keep_files=['molecular_identities.json'],boundary='Use the four complete named source molecules. Ph-mP and An-mP are the fixed representative pair for the detailed intervention. Use a common gas-phase baseline and identical fragment and state-energy definitions. Generate and record a complete atom mapping from the public names; no predicted high-triplet channel index is specified for autonomous research.',reference_definition='For a matched physical Tn, delta_STn=E(S1;R_S0)-E(Tn;R_S0). Report SOC norms in cm^-1 and neighboring Tn±1 spacings at the same geometry and Hamiltonian. Energy/SOC support necessary channel prerequisites; neither is an absolute RISC rate or quantum yield.',controls={'window':'Start at least five singlets and five triplets; enlarge to ten of each for representatives and further if the selected state lies at the boundary. Compare a common energy window containing S1 and neighboring candidate triplets.','geometry':'For Ph-mP and An-mP freeze the terminal-aromatic/phenylene linking torsion at 45 degrees, relax other S0 coordinates, and repeat the state/SOC window. Define the four mapped torsion atoms.','series':'After representative calibration, compute the relaxed-geometry state/SOC window for Na-mP and Py-mP using the same protocol.','competition':'For every candidate high-triplet channel report at least the two neighboring triplets and their character; near degeneracy or alternative localization may change the inference.'},panels={'series_states':panel(K(['Ph-mP','Na-mP','An-mP','Py-mP'],high),'Four-member matched state windows with high-state SOC','Check actual SOC matrix and NTO outputs; fragment weights must normalize consistently. Do not assume author Tn labels remain physical states when method or geometry changes.'),'representative_controls':panel(K(['Ph-mP','An-mP'],O(fixed_torsion=high,expanded_roots=high,root_overlap_file=PATH,torsion_atoms=A(I(1),4),torsion_deg=N(),evidence_files=EV)),'Representative root-window and geometry interventions','Require independent enlarged-window and frozen-torsion outputs. Root permutation is handled through state-density matching, not forced energy ordering.'),'channel_competition':panel(K(['Ph-mP','An-mP'],O(candidate_triplet_id=S(),neighbor_lower_id=S(),neighbor_upper_id=S(),candidate_gap_eV=N(),lower_spacing_eV=N(),upper_spacing_eV=N(),candidate_soc_cm1=N(minimum=0),alternative_channel_soc_cm1=N(minimum=0),CT_character_comparison_file=PATH,geometry_effect=PAIR,method_effect=PAIR,evidence_files=EV)),'Competing high-state channels and bounded inference','Compare direct coupling, energy proximity and state character together. Adjacent triplet internal conversion can compete even when S1/Tn gaps are small; its rate is not computed by a spacing. Accept rejection/ambiguity after the required evidence.')},investigations={'series_states':'Calibrate Ph-mP and An-mP first, then calculate the four-member window with states, oscillator strengths, transition densities and actual SOC pairs.','representative_controls':'For the two representatives enlarge the root set and repeat the fixed 45-degree terminal torsion, recording state overlap and changed gaps/couplings.','channel_competition':'Compare each representative candidate against neighboring triplets and a CT-sensitive method contrast; state what necessary conditions are supported and which kinetics remain unknown.'},author='Main pp3–5/Figure3 and SI TablesS1/NTO figures use Gaussian09W B3LYP/6-31G(d,p), gas-phase energies and Multiwfn fragment analysis. The authors discuss T4 channels for Ph/Na and T3 for An/Py. These indices are source assignments, not fixed targets under a changed method. Direct SOC matrices, root-window enlargement and frozen-torsion tests are new; they cannot by themselves establish an absolute hot-exciton/RISC yield.',pitfalls='Reject high-state selection solely by author index, absent SOC outputs, mismatched geometries/solvents, non-normalized fragment populations or a rate/efficiency inferred from a small gap alone.',optional='Nonadiabatic dynamics, absolute RISC rates and quantum efficiencies are optional.',source_note='Read main pp3–5/Figure3 and SI pp2–6 low/high-state table, NTO and IFCT definitions. Source gives energies and characters, not a calibrated full SOC/kinetic reference; a tabulated Py CT/LE percentage pair is internally inconsistent, so re-normalize from actual densities rather than copy it.',software='ORCA TDDFT/SOC with Gaussian baseline comparison; Multiwfn/transition-density analysis.',pilot='Demonstrate reproducible Ph-mP/An-mP state matching and high-state SOC with expanded roots before extending to Na/Py.',reference_gaps=['Expanded high-state SOC, geometry intervention and state-window/method uncertainty remain uncomputed.']))

