add(dict(id=pid,title='Test topology and substituent effects on open-shell character in four PAH models',objective='Determine how backbone topology and substituent changes affect open-shell character and low-energy optical states, separating relaxation and electronic effects with matched scaffolds and spin diagnostics.',objects={k:obj(f,0,(1,3),identity_file=k+'_identity.json') for k,f in [('1M_OMe','C56H42O2'),('1M_TIPS','C58H42Si2'),('2M_OMe','C58H44O2'),('2M_TIPS','C60H44Si2')]},boundary='Use four supplied mapped graph models with source truncation: long alkoxy chains are OMe and the label TIPS denotes the source C#C-SiH3 computational substitute, not full Si(iPr)3. Generate independent coordinates. 1M and 2M differ by C2H2; compare spin/optical observables, never their bare total energies. Oxidized 2M-prime is a different compound and outside this matrix.',reference_definition='Within each fixed composition report E(T)-E(CS) on shared CS geometry and separately at state-relaxed geometries. BS energies are determinant energies with S2/occupations, not a spin-pure singlet unless an explicitly justified projection is supplied. Across topologies compare like-defined gaps and state descriptors, not total E.',controls={'spin':'CS, independently initialized BS and triplet for all four models, with orbital stability and natural occupations. At least two BS starts and independent conformer starts; accept evidenced collapse.','shared_scaffold':'For each topology use the supplied common atom mapping between OMe and TIPS models. Fix mapped shared heavy scaffold to the OMe triplet geometry, relax only unmatched atoms, then compare states. Such frozen structures are not minima.','calibration':'For one most diagnostically ambiguous member chosen by occupation diagnostics, test a spin-adapted small-active-space or another documented independent electronic diagnostic before treating unrestricted TD states as definitive.','environment':'Use one common gas electronic-spin baseline and a consistently declared chloroform optical model. Keep excitation versus spin-energy comparisons separate.'},panels={'relaxed_series':panel(K(['1M_OMe','1M_TIPS','2M_OMe','2M_TIPS'],pahcell),'Four matched electronic-state and optical panels','Verify source model graphs, H counts and neutral spin spaces; inspect stability/occupation and TD evidence. The former 1M-TIPS geometry was not a new minimum validation.'),'frozen_scaffold':panel(K(['1M_OMe','1M_TIPS','2M_OMe','2M_TIPS'],O(reference_record=S(),scaffold_mapping_file=PATH,held_atoms_file=PATH,CS_record=S(),BS_record=S(),triplet_record=S(),T_minus_CS_eV=N(),natural_occupations=A(N(minimum=0),2),state_evidence_file=PATH,evidence_files=EV)),'Within-topology frozen-scaffold substituent controls','Check exact retained common scaffold coordinates and fragment valence; compare effects within each topology first. Frozen BS collapse is documented in its record, not a fabricated distinct solution.'),'calibrated_interpretation':panel(O(calibration_object=E(['1M_OMe','1M_TIPS','2M_OMe','2M_TIPS']),calibration_records=REF,active_space_or_independent_diagnostic=S(),diagnostic_file=PATH,topology_effect=PAIR,substituent_relaxation_effect=PAIR,electronic_model_effect=PAIR,evidence_files=EV),'Independent spin calibration and topology/substitution discrimination','Cross-check occupations, spin gaps and optical state character against an independent electronic model. An unrestricted instability or large oscillator strength does not alone prove a diradical assignment or experimental spectrum.')},investigations={'relaxed_series':'Build all four structures and evaluate stable CS, BS and triplet alternatives with conformer/collapse evidence; calculate matched low optical states in a consistent medium.','frozen_scaffold':'Generate common-scaffold interventions for both substitution pairs using the public mapped graph correspondence and evaluate electronic-state differences without borrowing equilibrium thermal corrections.','calibrated_interpretation':'Select one ambiguous representative by a recorded rule, perform independent spin calibration, and quantify topology/substituent/relaxation effects with a method sensitivity.'},author='The source uses B3LYP-D3/def2-SVP structures/frequencies and TD calculations with chloroform PCM. SI coordinates define 1M/2M methoxy and silyl-ethynyl computational models and include closed/open-shell alternatives. The authors relate extension to open-shell/optical changes. The benchmark adds consistent state competition and frozen-scaffold tests; it does not equate the different formulas of 1M and 2M.',pitfalls='Reject confusing full TIPS with SiH3 truncation, using oxidized 2M-prime as a conformer, raw cross-formula total-energy rankings, unvalidated BS minima or unsupported TD certainty under strong multireference character.',optional='Full alkyl groups, oxidation products, device performance and a large new molecular design series are optional.',source_note='Read main electronic/optical discussion and SI computational methods plus Cartesian blocks from p42 onward for four named models. Extracted graph-only identities; 1M versus 2M differs by C2H2. Closed-shell coordinate block provenance is private and does not assign a winner.',software='Gaussian/ORCA DFT/TDDFT, natural orbitals and available CASSCF/spin-adapted calibration; RDKit graph mapping.',pilot='Validate full 1M_OMe and one 2M spin-state set and common-scaffold map; inspect whether independent calibration is needed before full state matrix.',reference_gaps=['New state minima, common-scaffold interventions and diagnostic-calibrated optical references remain uncomputed.']))

