add(dict(id=pid,title='Separate metal-size, geometry and hydration effects on Ln–KHQ conformers',objective='Test whether La/Tb/Lu conformer preferences are explained by metal replacement, structural relaxation or explicit coordination water within a controlled 4f-core molecular model.',objects=lnobjs,keep_files=['syn_La_KHQ.xyz','anti_La_KHQ.xyz'],status='blocked',blockers=['Exact numerical Dolg 4f-core ECP and matching (7s6p5d)/[5s4p3d] basis files for La/Tb/Lu have not been verified or staged. Source core definitions are known, but BSE Stuttgart RLC metadata lacks these Ln entries and queried files are unavailable. Release requires verified molecular coefficients/core counts, or a documented alternative with equivalent-observable calibration.','No pilot has yet confirmed one source-model minimum and thermochemistry with the intended ECP; periodic pseudopotential availability does not resolve this gate.'],boundary='Use both complete La starting structures and replace only the metal for Tb/Lu. Preserve all 81 original atom IDs and ligand deprotonation (complex charge +1). For the one-water models append O82,H83,H84. Source 4f-core removes 46,54,60 electrons for La,Tb,Lu respectively, leaving 11 explicit neutral-atom electrons; all complex calculations use formal pseudo-singlet in this model. Do not describe Tb as physically spinless.',reference_definition='For each metal and identical hydration n, delta_G=G(anti,n)-G(syn,n) at 298 K, 1 M complexes in aqueous SMD. G=E_solv+(G_gas-E_gas) with consistent source low-frequency treatment, no double-counted ZPE. Water-addition delta_G=G(LnL.H2O)-G(LnL)-G(H2O) with 55.5 M water standard state. Frozen metal replacements compare electronic within-metal conformer gaps, not equilibrium G.',controls={'matrix':'Three metals x syn/anti x zero/one water; try at least two water directions and classify bound/lost water explicitly. If a bound state repeatedly collapses, retain that scientific result with structures and account for separated water in the reaction.','fixed_backbone':'At each dry La syn/anti geometry replace only the metal and compute Tb/Lu single points; compare frozen and relaxed within-metal gaps. Never compare raw different-metal energies.','water_cycle':'Close each syn/anti water-addition square: hydration effect on conformer gap equals difference of hydration free energies.','thermochemistry':'Source gas geometry/frequencies plus solution single points; use the same qRRHO cutoff/standard states and repeat a reasonable low-frequency treatment sensitivity.'},panels={'conformer_hydration_matrix':panel(K(['La','Tb','Lu'],K(['water0','water1'],gcell)),'Same-hydration three-metal conformer free energies','Verify exact ECP coefficients/core counts/explicit electron counts and original ligand charge. Inspect frequencies, qRRHO and standard states. A lost-water endpoint is an evidenced collapse/separated limit, not a falsely bound minimum.'),'replacement_and_cycles':panel(K(['La','Tb','Lu'],O(frozen_syn_record=S(),frozen_anti_record=S(),frozen_delta_E_kcal_mol=N(),relaxed_delta_E_kcal_mol=N(),syn_hydration_G_kcal_mol=N(),anti_hydration_G_kcal_mol=N(),cycle_closure_error_kcal_mol=N(),free_water_record=S(),evidence_files=EV)),'Frozen metal replacement and closed hydration squares','Recompute every balanced difference and cycle. Cross-metal raw total energies or unbalanced water counts cannot support selectivity. Frozen states use E only.'),'ecp_and_sensitivity':panel(O(metals=K(['La','Tb','Lu'],O(ecp_file=PATH,basis_file=PATH,core_electrons=I(),explicit_atom_electrons=C(11),basis_contraction=S(),hamiltonian=S(),test_record=S())),thermochemistry_sensitivity=PAIR,water_placement_records=REF,conformation_vs_hydration_file=PATH,evidence_files=EV),'Molecular ECP identity and low-frequency robustness','Audit source numerical ECP/basis and pseudo-spin before interpreting comparison. Install reports are not coefficient or pilot evidence. Check low-frequency sensitivity against small conformer gaps; do not transfer old La tolerance to Tb/Lu/hydration.')},investigations={'conformer_hydration_matrix':'Resolve the explicit ECP input gate; validate the dry/hydrated syn/anti models for all metals and report matched thermochemistry with collapse evidence where appropriate.','replacement_and_cycles':'Calculate dry frozen La-skeleton metal replacements and matched water-addition cycles; separate relaxation and hydration contributions to within-metal preferences.','ecp_and_sensitivity':'Audit ECP/basis electron counts and repeat the decisive low-frequency or solvation choice. Explain conformational trends only within the validated model.'},author='SI pp21–22 uses Gaussian16 omegaB97XD/def2-SVP on CHNO and Dolg large-core (46+4f^n electrons) ECP/(7s6p5d)/[5s4p3d] Ln basis. Gas geometries and frequencies are combined with SMD-water single points; GoodVibes uses Grimme low-frequency entropy with 100 cm^-1 cutoff, 298 K, 1 M complexes and 55.5 M water. Equations S1/S2/S3 distinguish water binding, anti-minus-syn and gas metal binding. Frozen-backbone and closed hydration-square tests are benchmark additions.',pitfalls='Reject small-core/all-electron calculations called equivalent without calibration, real Tb singlet claims from pseudo-spin, wrong ligand charge, cross-metal total-energy selectivity, unbalanced hydration or duplicated thermal corrections.',optional='Quantitative extraction/metal selectivity is outside scope without an independently closed metal hydration-exchange cycle; no full exchange cycle is mandatory here.',source_note='Read main pp3/5 and SI pp21–22 exact DFT/ECP/thermochemistry definitions and water equations. Checked 81-atom C32H38N4O6La+ start. Queried BSE metadata and molecular coefficients: Stuttgart RLC lists no La/Tb/Lu; coefficient requests failed. This specifically unresolved source-basis gate is retained, rather than treating QE/SIESTA pseudopotentials as molecular ECP evidence.',software='Gaussian/ORCA molecular ECP calculations, GoodVibes or independently checked thermochemistry; intended coefficient files remain a gate.',pilot='Stage and parse the three exact ECP/basis files, verify electron counts, then run one La minimum/frequency and one Tb single point before any expanded reference.',reference_gaps=['Verified numerical ECP/basis and pilot evidence are missing.','Expanded metal/hydration minima, thermochemical cycles and uncertainty remain uncomputed.']))

