add(dict(id=pid,title='Test metal–ligand contributions to a real Ir–Ir bond with paired truncation',objective='Determine whether metal–ligand orbital mixing is needed to explain the Ir–Ir bonding response, using full and exactly truncated dimers, fixed fragment definitions and distance/twist interventions.',objects={'Egan2Ir2':obj('C88H104Ir2N4O12',0,(1,3)),'egan2Ir2':obj('C56H40Ir2N4O12',0,(1,3)),'EganIr':obj('C44H52IrN2O6',0,(2,)),'eganIr':obj('C28H20IrN2O6',0,(2,))},boundary='Use Egan_identity.json and egan_identity.json for the true two-Ir dimers. Each ligand binds one Ir through its two iminoxolene N,O pairs; the ester oxygens are not assigned as donors in this dimer. Full Egan has four tert-butyl groups per ligand; truncated egan replaces exactly these with H and retains the ethylene-dianthranilate tether. Opposite local helicities define the A,C starting arrangement, but no final symmetry or distance is imposed. The former mononuclear cis-alpha/beta IrCl objects are excluded.',reference_definition='For neutral doublet fragments A=(ligand)Ir and B=(ligand)Ir: E_int=E_AB-E_A(frozen)-E_B(frozen); E_def=sum[E_fragment(frozen)-E_fragment(relaxed)]; E_assoc=E_int+E_def, kcal/mol. Keep fragment charge/spin, basis/BSSE and relativistic definitions identical. This operational decomposition is not a unique partition of metal–metal versus ligand pi bonding.',controls={'paired_truncation':'Compare full Egan2Ir2 and tert-butyl-deleted egan2Ir2, with common retained-heavy mapping. Do not substitute the much smaller Hap4Ir2 model as though it were this same truncation.','states':'For each dimer examine closed/BS singlet and triplet with stability and natural occupations; classify minimum versus saddle on each claimed state.','distance':'For each dimer take its selected equilibrium fragment geometries, then separate rigid fragments by +0.2 and +0.5 angstrom along Ir-Ir, keeping orientation fixed. Compute like-defined interaction and density/orbital descriptors.','twist':'At equilibrium distance rotate fragment B 30 degrees about Ir-Ir while keeping both fragments internally rigid; compare orbital mixing and interaction. These interventions need not be minima.','fragments':'Use neutral doublets and disclose fragment occupations; if another decomposition is scientifically needed it is a separate calibrated sensitivity, not a hidden replacement.'},panels={'dimer_states':panel(K(['Egan2Ir2','egan2Ir2'],ircell),'True dimers, electronic states and paired truncation','Check actual full/truncated graph/mapping, opposite-helicity starts, spin/occupation and curvature. Mononuclear energy differences are irrelevant to Ir–Ir bond validation. Do not force a source symmetry saddle into a minimum.'),'fragment_interventions':panel(K(['Egan2Ir2','egan2Ir2'],K(['equilibrium','distance_plus_0p2','distance_plus_0p5','twist_30'],frag)),'Fixed-fragment interaction/deformation and distance/twist matrix','Recompute fragment arithmetic; no missing ligand/metal atoms or state-dependent reference swaps. Examine basis superposition and scalar/SOC Hamiltonian choices. An energy decomposition alone does not uniquely isolate pi causation.'),'bonding_evidence':panel(O(retained_atom_mapping_file=PATH,orbital_population_grid_file=PATH,bond_order_grid_file=PATH,density_rearrangement_grid_file=PATH,truncation_effect=PAIR,twist_effect=PAIR,method_or_fragment_sensitivity=PAIR,evidence_files=EV),'Cross-check orbital, density, bond-index and energy explanations','Require correlated response to the explicit interventions in both model sizes and a real sensitivity. Accept direct-metal, ligand-assisted or indistinguishable explanations when evidence supports them; do not award a cartoon or single bond order as causal proof.')},investigations={'dimer_states':'Assemble full/truncated A,C dimers independently, test singlet/BS/triplet solutions and validate retained minima with spin/occupation evidence.','fragment_interventions':'Using the fixed neutral-doublet decomposition, calculate equilibrium and rigid distance/twist controls, fragment relaxation terms and density differences at both model sizes.','bonding_evidence':'Compare orbital mixing, densities, bond indices and interaction response to identify which explanations survive truncation and method/fragment sensitivity.'},author='Main pp7–9/Figures5–7 attributes a short Ir–Ir bond partly to ligand-assisted pi interactions. Source Gaussian B3LYP calculations use Ir SDD and 6-31G* light-atom basis and simplified Hap=1,2-C6H4(NH)O; the source (Hap)4Ir2 S4 structure is a minimum while constrained C2h is a first-order saddle. Full Egan2Ir2 is experimentally characterized. The benchmark Egan-to-egan paired tert-butyl truncation, neutral-doublet fragment energies and distance/twist interventions are new; Hap simplification cannot validate their values.',pitfalls='Reject one-Ir surrogates, Egan/egan/Hap truncations conflated, wrong fragment charge/spin, unsupported effective minima, or a unique pi-causality claim from a single bond index. Old E_beta-E_alpha=-0.162283 kcal/mol is not an Ir–Ir bond energy.',optional='Hap4Ir2 calibration, all oxidation states and large-scale dynamics are optional; licensed EDA is not mandatory.',source_note='Read main synthesis formula C44H52N2O6 and full dimer C88H104Ir2N4O12, computational section p3 and bonding pp7–9; SI pp27–30 contains Hap4Ir2 (54-atom) structures, not full/truncated Egan dimer references. Prepared named full graph and exactly four tBu-to-H deletions per ligand, checked formulas. This supplies an implementable new pair while preserving the missing-pilot limitation.',software='Gaussian/ORCA DFT, fragment single points and wavefunction analysis; Multiwfn and available multireference diagnostic if necessary.',pilot='Validate one full/truncated pair and neutral fragment doublets, source-relativity consistency and state stability before distance/twist scans.',reference_gaps=['No full/truncated Egan dimer minimum, fragment decomposition or multi-reference calibration has been computed.','Source Hap reference is a different truncation and cannot certify this new paired model.']))

